   "fix": "Replace \"upstream\" with a provenance-neutral phrase such as \"the general `PDF` API in `EpsilonEridani.Particles.Parton.PDF`\" / \"the species-level bundle `PDF.SumRuleAssumptions`\" at each of those lines; reserve \"upstream\" for Mathlib/Physlib/TauCeti material (as e.g. `Mathematics/KroneckerDelta/BasicExtensions.lean:22` does).",
   "issue": "The `PDF.*` API is described as \"upstream\" throughout, but none of it is upstream: `Assumptions`, `SumRuleAssumptions`, `weight`, `modelPdf`, `valenceNumber`, `sumRuleAssumptionsWeightModelPdfZeroOne` all live in `EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/PDF/*`, and `PDF.weight` plus `PDF.sumRuleAssumptionsWeightModelPdfZeroOne` are added by this very PR. Occurrences: lines 18, 19, 20, 34, 50-51, 55, 65, 72, 267, 323, 336, 377, and `Particles/Parton/PDF/Model.lean:228` (\"carries the upstream sum-rule bundle\").",
   "line": 51
  }
